        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">As discussed in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3623204721" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41938" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/41938/hovercard?comment_id=3530152718&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41938#issuecomment-3530152718">#41938 (comment)</a> , response headers should not have the section on "forbidden request headers". I have modified this so that response headers listed in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3623204721" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41938" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/41938/hovercard?comment_id=3530227774&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41938#issuecomment-3530227774">#41938 (comment)</a> now have "Forbidden response header" instead.</p>
<p dir="auto">I also updated the request and response headers to include the forbidden response information.</p>]]></content>
